{"nodes": [{"id": "memories_architecture_guide_architecture_guide", "label": "Architecture Guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".serena/memories/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "memories_architecture_guide_layered_architecture", "label": "Five-Layer Architecture (Client/API/Service/Repository/Data)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".serena/memories/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "## Layered Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client (React/Zustand/TanStack Query) \u2192 API (Next.js routes + tRPC) \u2192 Service (business logic + integrations) \u2192 Repository (Prisma wrapper) \u2192 Data (PostgreSQL); each layer only talks to the one below, isolating framework, logic, and persistence concerns."}, {"id": "memories_architecture_guide_repository_pattern", "label": "Repository Pattern (server/repository)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".serena/memories/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "## Repository Pattern", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven repositories abstract Prisma access from business logic and convert snake_case DB rows to camelCase domain types (toDomain), so services never depend on Prisma column naming."}, {"id": "memories_architecture_guide_challenge_security", "label": "Challenge-Based Mutation Security", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".serena/memories/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "## Security", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Protected mutations require a server-issued challenge token, client proof-of-work, a one-time nonce (replay prevention), and a request hash (integrity), sent as X-Challenge-* headers; PoW deters bots without user accounts."}], "edges": [{"source": "memories_arc